      "cols_json": {},
      "parent_index": null,
      "last_updated": "2026-05-12T00:00:00.000000",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "About",
      "order": 6,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Ten sections of a mouse head (brain, eye, nasal cavity), stained with hematoxylin and eosin and scanned at 0.45 um: 55296 x 96000 pixels, about 16 GB at full resolution. The slide is read in place from JAX's public OME-Zarr copy; each tile only fetches the pieces of the pyramid it shows. The overview on the left draws the tissue cut into 500 um patches, coloured by how densely nucleated each one is. Draw a rectangle or a lasso over some patches (or click one) and the detail view on the right zooms to them at full resolution, where single nuclei are visible; the plots and the table follow the same patches. The section filter does the same for a whole section. Slide from the JAX KOMP histopathology collection (CC BY 4.0); the patch table is computed from the slide by colour deconvolution (dev/bioimage/make_wsi_patches.py).\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
